1.m:
The holy Lord said:
Listen, O Goddess, I shall explain what you ask of me;
by merely hearing it, one becomes dear to the yoginīs.

the pair 'gṛhṇa', the word 'ruru', then the word 'kṣetrapāla';
one should utter 'sarvopacārasahitāmimāṃ pūjāṃ baliṃ',
'gṛhṇa gṛhṇa' ending with two ṭhas (svāhā)—this is the mantra of the guardian of the sacred field, O dear one.

In the west [one should present the offering to] the god Baṭuka, in the north the offering to the yoginīs,
in the east one should give the offering to the spirits, and the guardian of the sacred field in the south;
one should worship Rājarājeśvara in the center, O leader of Kula.

The offering to the spirits is proclaimed with all the fingers, O dear one;
the offering to the guardian of the sacred field is made with the thumb and forefinger,
and that of Rājarājeśvara with the thumb and middle finger.
